+# Scenario: date-fns-french-ordinal-architecture
+
+## Source Issue
+
+French long-month formatting currently emits an extra ordinal suffix:
+
+- Expected: `jeudi 29 août 2019`
+- Actual: `jeudi 29ème août 2019`
+
+The issue appears when formatting with `iiii do MMMM yyyy`.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Fix production source, not the regression test.
+- Do not use the upstream PR patch, oracle commit, or live GitHub.
+- Do not edit package manifests, lockfiles, generated files, or this task file.
+- Do not edit `vitest.config.ts` or any other validation-only configuration.
+- Do not solve this as a final-output string replacement.
+- Prefer an extensible formatting/locale path that can support context-sensitive locale behavior.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+npx tsx src/format/agentflow-realworld-fr-ordinal/check.ts
+```
+
+## Agentflow Output Contract
+
+Write `handoff.md` in `$AGENTFLOW_OUTPUT_DIR` with:
+- `Scenario:` date-fns-french-ordinal-architecture
+- `Issue:` one-sentence summary
+- `Changed files:` exact files changed
+- `Validation:` exact command and result
+- `Risks:` remaining uncertainty or `none`
